<title>KENYA: Kenya tea prices mixed at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Kenya tea prices mixed at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>MOMBASA 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kenyan tea prices were mixed at the weekly auction in Mombasa on Monday as demand for good quality eased, auction officials said.</p>
<p>Brighter BP1s eased by 4-9 U.S cents while Brightest PF1s eased 10-15 cents. Lower mediums were firm while Brighter Pdusts were irregularly dearer. Selected bright liquoring Dust1s were also irregularly dearer.</p>
<p>Fannings and dusts held steady.</p>
<p>There was less enquiry from Pakistan and Egypt, while Sudan lent good support.</p>
<p>--Wambui Chege, Nairobi Newsroom ++254-2 330-261</p>
</text>
